</div>

</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-a26d900 e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-835b006 " data-id="a26d900" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="a26d900">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-9b1820a e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="9b1820a" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-94e171c elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="94e171c" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<h5 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">19 November 2026 -  Planning update</h5>				</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-3bc4be3 e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-b4df0c3 " data-id="3bc4be3" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="3bc4be3">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-e90ce87 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="e90ce87" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
		<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-9939752 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child" data-id="9939752" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-b28ce2e elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="b28ce2e" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p><strong>Plan A — Community leisure</strong></p><p>Our first choice is to use our land at Goring Gap for community leisure, with the facilities we need to look after it. At the heart of our plans is a large, tree-shaded sandpit where children can play and families, neighbours and visitors can spend time together outdoors.</p><p>We also propose overnight camping to support local tourism, a solar-powered barn to house the electric tractors we would use to maintain the site, and tree planting to improve biodiversity.</p><p>Worthing Borough Council’s Planning Committee, chaired by <a href="https://democracy.adur-worthing.gov.uk/mgUserInfo.aspx?UID=470" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Helen Abrahams</a>, voted unanimously to oppose our appeal, which is now with the Planning Inspectorate. Helen&#8217;s words were &#8216;anywhere but here&#8217;. If the appeal is unsuccessful and we go on to apply for affordable housing, the planning record will show that we first sought to use the land for community leisure.</p><p><strong>Plan B — Affordable housing and accommodation for refugees</strong></p><p>If our current planning proposals are unsuccessful, our next planning application will be for affordable housing and to explore whether the site could also accommodate a hostel for refugees. We would aim to power the development with renewable energy and design the homes to exceed the minimum energy performance needed for an EPC A rating.</p><p>The July 2025 Strategic Housing Market Assessment estimated that Worthing needs <strong>493 affordable homes a year</strong>. Worthing Borough Council’s Annual Monitoring Report recorded <strong>23 affordable homes completed in 2024/25</strong>. We believe affordable housing would be the best alternative use of our land and could help meet that local need. <a href="https://www.adur-worthing.gov.uk/media/Media%2C173487%2Csmxx.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Strategic Housing Market Assessment</a> · <a href="https://www.adur-worthing.gov.uk/media/Media%2C174297%2Csmxx.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Annual Monitoring Report</a></p><p>We understand that a public sewer was laid beneath Goring Gap in 1930 and was designed to serve up to 2,000 homes. We would ask Southern Water to confirm whether the network has enough capacity today to serve the proposed development. <a href="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/drains/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read about the sewer</a></p><p>Our understanding is that the covenants affecting our land limit residential development to a maximum of 33 detached homes. We would explore whether those covenants could be changed to allow up to 80 affordable terraced homes for local people, each with its own garden, parking space and secure bicycle storage. The site offers views towards the sea and the South Downs. We have already had a productive meeting with a local housing charity, and any housing proposal would require planning permission. <a href="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/covenants/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the covenants</a></p><p>A refugee hostel would depend on securing the necessary approvals and finding a suitable operator. We believe every family deserves a safe place to stay and a warm bed for the night. We want Worthing to be known as an inclusive town that welcomes people of all faiths and backgrounds and supports those who need help.</p><p>We know people feel strongly about the future of Goring Gap and are constantly watching what we do. We welcome different views and hope the discussion can stay respectful and focused on the proposals.</p>								</div>
				</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-344d06d e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-b8da0e7 " data-id="344d06d" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="344d06d">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-1a8c7f2 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="1a8c7f2" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
