				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-15eda9a e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-600bb90 " data-id="15eda9a" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="15eda9a">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-31ae4ee e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="31ae4ee" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-ab833a8 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="ab833a8" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<h5 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">26 August 2026 - Worthing's finest cars on show.</h5>				</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-4585bdd e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-041916e " data-id="4585bdd" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="4585bdd">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-9892ebd e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="9892ebd" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-2fad83b elementor-widget elementor-widget-image" data-id="2fad83b" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="image.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
																<a href="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Rolls-scaled.jpg" target="_blank">
							<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="768" height="576" src="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Rolls-768x576.jpg" class="attachment-medium_large size-medium_large wp-image-3983" alt="" srcset="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Rolls-768x576.jpg 768w, https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Rolls-300x225.jpg 300w, https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Rolls-1024x768.jpg 1024w, https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Rolls-1536x1152.jpg 1536w, https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Rolls-2048x1536.jpg 2048w" sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px" />								</a>
															</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-3e1126c e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-c41386c " data-id="3e1126c" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="3e1126c">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-b1fc269 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="b1fc269" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-abc9380 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="abc9380" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p class="PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer" data-start="96" data-end="260">We’re delighted to announce that we have been approached to host our very first car meet at Goring Gap, taking place on <strong data-start="220" data-end="259">Saturday 19th September from 6.30pm</strong>.</p><p data-start="262" data-end="618">We’re hoping it will be a great evening for car enthusiasts, families and anyone who simply enjoys seeing an interesting collection of vehicles in a relaxed seafront setting. Whether you have a classic car, performance car, sports car, something unusual or you would simply like to come along and have a look, everyone in the community is very welcome.</p><p data-start="620" data-end="734">Entry will be completely free, and we will also be offering free on-site parking, subject to availability.</p><p data-start="736" data-end="949">Our aim is for this to be a friendly, respectful and enjoyable gathering where people can meet, talk cars, enjoy the atmosphere and hopefully watch another spectacular Goring Gap sunset from our ringside position.</p><p data-start="951" data-end="1163">Our usual refreshments and facilities will be available throughout the evening, so come down, grab a drink, have a wander around and enjoy what we hope will become another enjoyable community event at Goring Gap.</p><p data-start="1165" data-end="1293"><strong data-start="1165" data-end="1192">Saturday 19th September</strong><br data-start="1192" data-end="1195" /><strong data-start="1195" data-end="1210">From 6.30pm</strong><br data-start="1210" data-end="1213" /><strong data-start="1213" data-end="1227">Free entry</strong><br data-start="1227" data-end="1230" /><strong data-start="1230" data-end="1270">Free parking subject to availability</strong><br data-start="1270" data-end="1273" /><strong data-start="1273" data-end="1293">Everyone welcome</strong></p><p>A big thank you to the owner of the beautiful Rolls-Royce pictured above, who is a regular visitor to Goring Gap. If you’re reading this, please bring her down on the 19th — she’s absolutely magnificent and we would love her to be at our first car meet!</p>								</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-3c1e381 e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-f96cedd " data-id="3c1e381" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="3c1e381">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-9624272 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="9624272" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-70a4d93 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="70a4d93" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<h5 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">15 August 2026 - for customers who choose to ride - we salute you! </h5>				</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-f58b8e1 e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-7f2897b " data-id="f58b8e1" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="f58b8e1">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-14d9f86 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="14d9f86" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-36407b7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image" data-id="36407b7" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="image.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
																<a href="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/IMG_9755-scaled.jpg" target="_blank">
							<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="768" height="576" src="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/IMG_9755-768x576.jpg" class="attachment-medium_large size-medium_large wp-image-3915" alt="" srcset="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/IMG_9755-768x576.jpg 768w, https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/IMG_9755-300x225.jpg 300w, https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/IMG_9755-1024x768.jpg 1024w, https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/IMG_9755-1536x1152.jpg 1536w, https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/IMG_9755-2048x1536.jpg 2048w" sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px" />								</a>
															</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-1731806 e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-6ddcba9 " data-id="1731806" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="1731806">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-76ea7c2 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="76ea7c2" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-2b787ff elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="2b787ff" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p class="PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer" data-start="118" data-end="287">We were proud to welcome so many cyclists today, many from Arundel and beyond. We are always delighted to see our car park quiet and bicycles stacked everywhere instead!</p><p data-start="289" data-end="618">As an environmentally conscious business, we go out of our way to reduce our impact wherever we can — using green energy, recycling, reducing waste and supporting biodiversity across our site. We are particularly proud that we now use no fossil fuels anywhere at Goring Gap, with our entire operation powered by green energy.</p><p data-start="620" data-end="948">It was wonderful to see groups arriving throughout the day, taking a well-earned break, using our clean toilet facilities, enjoying a drink, socialising with friends and family, and making the most of our beautiful seafront setting — and, of course, our ringside position for another one of Goring Gap’s spectacular sunsets!</p><p data-start="950" data-end="1228">One of our ambitions for Goring Gap has always been to create a welcoming place where walkers, cyclists, families, kite surfers, sea swimmers, with a large naturally shaded childrens sandpit, a tumbledown mound, boules area and showers planned for the future. A place where visitors to our great town can stop, relax and enjoy this very special part of Worthing; a place where world champions live.</p><p data-start="1230" data-end="1417">Seeing people deliberately making Goring Gap part of their route is incredibly encouraging and another reminder of just how much potential this area has as a destination in its own right.</p><p data-start="1419" data-end="1581" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Thank you to everyone who stopped by today. Whether you arrived on two wheels, two feet or four wheels, you were very welcome — and we hope to see you again soon.</p>								</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-415e117 e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-3dfc7cc " data-id="415e117" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="415e117">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-e639539 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="e639539" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-215b33c elementor-widget elementor-widget-image" data-id="215b33c" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="image.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
																<a href="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/IMG_9760-scaled.jpg" target="_blank">
							<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="768" height="576" src="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/IMG_9760-768x576.jpg" class="attachment-medium_large size-medium_large wp-image-3916" alt="" srcset="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/IMG_9760-768x576.jpg 768w, https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/IMG_9760-300x225.jpg 300w, https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/IMG_9760-1024x768.jpg 1024w, https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/IMG_9760-1536x1152.jpg 1536w, https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/IMG_9760-2048x1536.jpg 2048w" sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px" />								</a>
															</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-047c0ea e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-a2dfd9b " data-id="047c0ea" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="047c0ea">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-5bb8c40 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="5bb8c40" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-2cac34e elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="2cac34e" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<h5 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">14 August 2026 - Sound </h5>				</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-4292f64 e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-a9f2364 " data-id="4292f64" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="4292f64">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-cb1883d e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="cb1883d" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-0c8e6f0 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="0c8e6f0" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p class="isSelectedEnd">One of our surprise hits this summer has been <strong>Sound</strong>, the low-alcohol beer from Lakedown Brewing Co.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">Lakedown is based among the rolling hills of East Sussex on the family farm of actor and rock legend <strong>Roger Daltrey</strong>, and is home not only to the brewery but also to trout fishing lakes that helped inspire the business.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">It is very much a Sussex family affair. The brewery is run by Roger’s son Jamie, together with his sons-in-law Des and Chris.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">From the outset, their aim has been simple: to produce genuinely good versions of the beer styles they themselves enjoy drinking, without compromising on taste or quality.</p><p>We particularly like <strong>Sound</strong> because it proves that choosing a lower-alcohol beer doesn’t have to mean sacrificing flavour — and judging by how popular it has been with our customers, quite a few people at Goring Gap agree with us.</p>								</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-2bbb14e e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-e6c98b5 " data-id="2bbb14e" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="2bbb14e">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-7913520 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="7913520" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-21aa23b elementor-widget elementor-widget-image" data-id="21aa23b" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="image.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
																<a href="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Sound.webp">
							<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="300" height="240" src="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Sound-300x240.webp" class="attachment-medium size-medium wp-image-3897" alt="" srcset="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Sound-300x240.webp 300w, https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Sound-1024x819.webp 1024w, https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Sound-768x614.webp 768w, https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Sound-1536x1229.webp 1536w, https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Sound.webp 2048w" sizes="(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px" />								</a>
															</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-87a8c48 e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-c808f8a " data-id="87a8c48" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="87a8c48">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-f4f8254 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="f4f8254" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-bda0011 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="bda0011" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<h5 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">13 August 2026 - A big thank you!</h5>				</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-95b2094 e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-cc3553c " data-id="95b2094" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="95b2094">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-4c61f5e e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="4c61f5e" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-ef65b08 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="ef65b08" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p class="PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer" data-start="281" data-end="301">What an evening!</p><p data-start="303" data-end="462">Hundreds of people joined us yesterday to watch the eclipse. Our car park was full, we quite literally sold out of everything, and we had our best day yet.</p><p data-start="464" data-end="702">We were delighted to be able to give our customers free certified eclipse glasses, and it was wonderful to see so many people enjoying what, for many, will have been a once-in-a-lifetime experience. The weather could not have been better.</p><p data-start="704" data-end="819">A huge thank you to all our staff, especially Martin and Martha, who worked incredibly hard throughout the evening.</p><p data-start="821" data-end="955">It’s Martha’s very first job, and after yesterday we told her she can now genuinely put on her CV: “Works well under pressure.” 😄</p><p data-start="957" data-end="1106">And finally, thank you to everyone who came down and supported us. Seeing so many people enjoying Goring Gap on such a special evening was fantastic.</p><p data-start="1108" data-end="1182">Thank you again for your continued support — it really is appreciated.</p>								</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-cfe5442 e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-7bec15b " data-id="cfe5442" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="cfe5442">
    		<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-d7adf08 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image" data-id="d7adf08" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="image.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
																<a href="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Eclipse-actual.png">
							<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="768" height="576" src="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Eclipse-actual-768x576.png" class="attachment-medium_large size-medium_large wp-image-3801" alt="" srcset="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Eclipse-actual-768x576.png 768w, https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Eclipse-actual-300x225.png 300w, https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Eclipse-actual-1024x768.png 1024w, https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Eclipse-actual.png 1448w" sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px" />								</a>
															</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-cd4720b e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-c8f87f8 " data-id="cd4720b" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="cd4720b">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-52d97f4 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="52d97f4" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-81d2f04 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="81d2f04" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<h5 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">11 August 2026 - Chris Dixon to tender for West Buildings Shelter </h5>				</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-30cf8fc e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-a3e1c42 " data-id="30cf8fc" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="30cf8fc">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-e5e571f e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="e5e571f" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-1c84d6e elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="1c84d6e" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p class="isSelectedEnd">Chris Dixon has today announced his intention to tender for the West Building Shelter. Details <a href="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Pebble-Beach-Cafe-EOI-round-1-submission-final-draft2.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">here</a></p><p class="isSelectedEnd">Chris said: “As with Goring Gap, I believe it is possible to take a neglected and run-down (see <a href="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/pictures/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">here</a>) part of Worthing and create something positive that both visitors and the wider community can use and enjoy.</p><p>For years the shelter has stood empty and unused, which is completely unacceptable. Worthing’s promenade is one of the town’s greatest assets and, in my view, one of the finest stretches of seafront in Europe. We should be ambitious about what we create along it and make sure that the businesses operating there add something genuinely positive to the town.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">I believe our proposal will stand out not simply because of what we want to create, but because of how it will look and how sensitively it will sit within its surroundings. Our ambition is to create a building that is attractive, environmentally responsible and sympathetic to Worthing’s seafront character. I would like somebody visiting Worthing for the first time to look at the finished café and assume it has been part of the promenade for years.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">Our aim would be to celebrate and promote the very best that Sussex has to offer, while creating an attractive and welcoming destination for local residents and visitors alike.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">We are already developing products specifically around that vision. For example, we now have our own coffee beans under the brand name <strong>Sussex Gold</strong>, with the brand having been approved by the Intellectual Property Office.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">Our business at Goring Gap is deliberately seasonal, and we now need a permanent, year-round home for our business and, importantly, for our amazing team of staff.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">I believe the Pebble Beach Café could provide that opportunity.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">Just as we have done at Goring Gap, our ambition would be to demonstrate that a modern hospitality business can operate responsibly and sustainably. We would aim to make the Pebble Beach Café a fully carbon-neutral, green-energy business, while supporting local producers, creating employment opportunities and bringing new life to an important part of Worthing’s seafront.</p><p>Goring Gap has shown what can be achieved with a little imagination, investment and determination (click <a href="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/IMG_9343-scaled.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">here</a> and <a href="https://ratings.food.gov.uk/business-search?business-name-search=Goring+gap&amp;address-search=Worthing&amp;business_type=-1&amp;country_or_la=all&amp;hygiene_rating=all&amp;range=Equal&amp;hygiene_status=all" target="_blank" rel="noopener">here</a>) I believe, with all my teams experience, we could do something equally special at the West Buildings Shelter — creating a permanent home for our business while helping to breathe new life into another part of Worthing.”</p><p>Click on the image below to enlarge. We believe even our fiercest critics, including Susan Belton from The Worthing Society, who has certainly never been afraid to challenge any development in Worthing, will find it very difficult to fault our designs.</p>								</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-feb8f54 e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-fb4d9a3 " data-id="feb8f54" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="feb8f54">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-e5850e4 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="e5850e4" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-4703d35 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image" data-id="4703d35" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="image.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
																<a href="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/West-Building-Cafe-scaled.png" target="_blank">
							<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="768" height="543" src="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/West-Building-Cafe-768x543.png" class="attachment-medium_large size-medium_large wp-image-3706" alt="" srcset="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/West-Building-Cafe-768x543.png 768w, https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/West-Building-Cafe-300x212.png 300w, https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/West-Building-Cafe-1024x723.png 1024w, https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/West-Building-Cafe-1536x1085.png 1536w, https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/West-Building-Cafe-2048x1447.png 2048w" sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px" />								</a>
															</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-f1fab00 e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-46491a7 " data-id="f1fab00" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="f1fab00">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-49dac09 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="49dac09" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-9345f7c elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="9345f7c" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<h5 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">10 August 2026 - Hold an Eclipse at the Eclipse! </h5>				</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-eac7dad e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-d7e1975 " data-id="eac7dad" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="eac7dad">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-0bcebdc e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="0bcebdc" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-c6f610d elementor-widget elementor-widget-image" data-id="c6f610d" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="image.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
															<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="225" height="300" src="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Eclipse-Can-1-768x1024-1-225x300.png" class="attachment-medium size-medium wp-image-3682" alt="" srcset="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Eclipse-Can-1-768x1024-1-225x300.png 225w, https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Eclipse-Can-1-768x1024-1.png 768w" sizes="(max-width: 225px) 100vw, 225px" />															</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-b71b92a e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-faa5b11 " data-id="b71b92a" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="b71b92a">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-b66adb6 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="b66adb6" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-e98c523 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="e98c523" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p>As many of you know we only supply and promote local beer and spirits. Please allow me to introduce Langham Brewery. They are nestled in the heart of the South Downs National Park and been brewing award-winning beer since 2005 from an 18th-century granary barn in Lodsworth, West Sussex.</p><p>We are proud to promote their fantastic products, of which is their amazing Eclipse Porter. So come down and hold an Eclipse in your hand while you watch a lifetime memory Eclipse. Take the empty tin home with you and write the place and date on the underside to remember the moment.</p>								</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-3806364 e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-f67fd3f " data-id="3806364" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="3806364">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-377b396 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="377b396" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-2a9774e elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="2a9774e" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<h5 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">07 August 2026 - Enlarged entrance for caravans and motorhomes</h5>				</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-f3fa3d7 e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-e8c55a6 " data-id="f3fa3d7" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="f3fa3d7">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-f2e5d67 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="f2e5d67" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-99f9960 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="99f9960" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p class="isSelectedEnd">As part of our planning application, West Sussex County Council Highways has requested that the site entrance be widened to allow cars and campervans to enter and leave simultaneously. They have also asked for dedicated staff parking, and cycle store facilities.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">We have therefore instructed our architects to prepare the necessary drawings for submission.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">We would genuinely welcome any constructive design suggestions from local residents. Please use the contact button above. We read every objection submitted and carefully consider the valid issues raised.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">We particularly enjoyed the following comment from a Ferring resident:</p><p class="isSelectedEnd"><em>“Use of land to produce natural green energy, for example solar. Exact details needed. Size, quantity, possible noise from turbines. Turbine noise could disturb nesting birds, especially skylarks.”</em></p><p class="isSelectedEnd">We can confirm that our solar panels have no moving parts and produce no turbine noise. They are therefore highly unlikely to disturb nesting skylarks.</p><p>For the avoidance of doubt, no wind turbines are proposed as part of our application.</p>								</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-5c12e8d e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-8eda08c " data-id="5c12e8d" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="5c12e8d">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-5064425 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="5064425" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-74b9abc elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="74b9abc" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<h5 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">06 August 2026 - Partial Eclipse</h5>				</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-2e0db83 e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-c3db844 " data-id="2e0db83" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="2e0db83">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-a8f079b e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="a8f079b" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-78baa55 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image" data-id="78baa55" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="image.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
																<a href="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/sundowners-final.png" target="_blank">
							<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="576" src="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/sundowners-final-1024x576.png" class="attachment-large size-large wp-image-3593" alt="" srcset="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/sundowners-final-1024x576.png 1024w, https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/sundowners-final-300x169.png 300w, https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/sundowners-final-768x432.png 768w, https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/sundowners-final-1536x864.png 1536w, https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/sundowners-final.png 1672w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" />								</a>
															</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-8b30cd3 e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-86488d6 " data-id="8b30cd3" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="8b30cd3">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-f3fc864 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="f3fc864" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-a03213c elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="a03213c" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p class="PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer" data-start="0" data-end="71">Enjoy uninterrupted views of the partial solar eclipse from Goring Gap.</p><p data-start="73" data-end="387">The photograph above shows the actual view of the Sun setting over the South Downs, taken from our land by us. It also illustrates exactly what is at stake. If our land were ever developed for housing, our neighbour could seek to develop their land too—and this remarkable open view could disappear forever.</p><p data-start="389" data-end="643">That is why the suggestion, repeated by some people on online, that we want to build houses here is not only wrong but completely illogical. Our aim is to protect this incredible landscape, keep the land open and create a place that the whole community can enjoy.</p><p data-start="645" data-end="935">So come down to one of the best viewing locations in Worthing. Relax with a local craft beer, a glass of wine or a cocktail as the Moon passes across the Sun, before watching the Sun set over the South Downs. You will be hard-pushed to find a better ringside seat for this remarkable event.</p><p data-start="937" data-end="1150">We have on-site parking for up to 150 cars, together with our own toilet facilities. The public toilets across the road are not maintained adequately and are unhygienic. They also close a 7pm. We will also have a limited supply of free certified eclipse glasses available to customers on a first-come, first-served basis.</p><p data-start="1152" data-end="1329" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Please remember that ordinary sunglasses are not safe for viewing an eclipse. Always use certified eclipse glasses or another approved solar viewer when looking towards the Sun.</p>								</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-d93be16 e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-3868e81 " data-id="d93be16" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="d93be16">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-36be908 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="36be908" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-edfb678 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="edfb678" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<h5 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">05 August 2026 - Brooklands Park Comparison Statement </h5>				</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-631ce4d e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-ca665e8 " data-id="631ce4d" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="631ce4d">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-f6d6424 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="f6d6424" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-b648bbe elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="b648bbe" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p class="isSelectedEnd">We have again contacted Worthing Borough Council to ask why our previously submitted Brooklands Park Comparison Statement remains unpublished on the planning application file.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">This is particularly concerning because further negative representations have continued to be accepted and published after the consultation deadline of 16 July, while our detailed response addressing important planning, legal and factual comparisons has still not been made publicly available.</p><p>We have asked the Council to explain the reason for this apparent imbalance and to publish our statement without further delay.<br /><br />Our Brooklands Park Comparison Statement was submitted to Worthing Borough Council in July as part of our planning application.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">The Worthing Local Plan identifies four designated Gaps. Brooklands Park and Goring Gap are two of them. The Council must therefore explain, in clear planning and legal terms, why comparable community, leisure and visitor facilities appear to be treated so differently.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">At Brooklands Park, the Council has previously approved:</p><ul data-spread="false"><li><strong>AWDM/1537/22 (2022):</strong> the temporary siting of a storage container for nine months of each year, from April to December, for the storage of kites, paddleboards and associated equipment connected with a seafront kitesurf school concession.</li><li><strong>AWDM/1843/21 (2021):</strong> the demolition of an existing toilet block and the construction of a new café and public toilets, together with a plant and refuse room, accessible play area, landscaping and bicycle storage. This application varied the design and size of the café and toilet building previously approved under <strong>AWDM/0266/20</strong>.</li></ul><p class="isSelectedEnd">These were not hypothetical proposals. The Council accepted temporary storage facilities, commercial leisure activity and the construction of a permanent café and visitor facilities within Brooklands Park.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">Our application at Goring Gap seeks permission for seasonal, community-focused leisure use involving predominantly temporary and non-permanent facilities.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">The obvious question is therefore:</p><p class="isSelectedEnd"><strong>Why is a temporary storage container acceptable within one designated Gap but potentially unacceptable within another?</strong></p><p class="isSelectedEnd"><strong>Why is it legally and environmentally acceptable to demolish a toilet block and construct a permanent café at Brooklands Park, yet objection is raised to a seasonal, non-permanent café and community leisure facilities at Goring Gap?</strong></p><p class="isSelectedEnd">Planning decisions must be based on evidence, adopted policy and consistent planning principles. Two designated Gaps cannot simply be treated differently without a clear and legally defensible planning justification.</p><p>If Worthing Borough Council refuses our application, it will need to define precisely what material planning distinction justifies that difference in treatment. Should the matter proceed to appeal, it may ultimately fall to the independent Planning Inspectorate to determine whether that distinction is lawful, reasonable and supported by the Council’s own planning policies and previous decisions.</p>								</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-2e5a585 e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-dfe3002 " data-id="2e5a585" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="2e5a585">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-098082c e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="098082c" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-c8e3bdd elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="c8e3bdd" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<h5 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">03 August 2026 - Ideas for 2027</h5>				</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-7438741 e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-1a270d4 " data-id="7438741" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="7438741">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-a55db1d e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="a55db1d" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-aadb9f4 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="aadb9f4" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p class="PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer" data-start="66" data-end="231">Our current season will come to an end at the close of next month. Everything will then be removed from the site, leaving it once again as a clear, open green field.</p><p data-start="233" data-end="446">Subject to planning permission being granted for the land to be used for community leisure activities, we will soon be inviting local residents, community groups and organisations to help shape our plans for 2027.</p><p data-start="448" data-end="779">We are open to imaginative ideas, but we have several important principles. Any proposed activity must be environmentally responsible and support the work we have already undertaken to promote renewable energy, sustainability and biodiversity. It must also be community-focused, inclusive and appropriate for this special location.</p><p data-start="781" data-end="1023">We are particularly interested in ideas that create opportunities for younger people, as well as older residents—many of whom may no longer have access to a garden or meaningful outdoor space as a result of downsizing or changes in lifestyle.</p><p data-start="1025" data-end="1321">Suggestions might include activities that encourage gentle exercise, improve physical and mental wellbeing, bring different generations together, teach practical environmental skills, support local creativity or simply give people more opportunities to enjoy the outdoors and connect with others.</p><p data-start="1323" data-end="1362">We would especially welcome ideas that:</p><ul data-start="1364" data-end="1832"><li data-section-id="hlbbvb" data-start="1364" data-end="1411">Bring younger and older generations together.</li><li data-section-id="1nsnxw" data-start="1412" data-end="1462">Support health, happiness and social connection.</li><li data-section-id="1142n8v" data-start="1463" data-end="1505">Encourage people to spend time outdoors.</li><li data-section-id="1clr92h" data-start="1506" data-end="1550">Promote nature, wildlife and biodiversity.</li><li data-section-id="ln52x9" data-start="1551" data-end="1608">Use renewable energy or demonstrate sustainable living.</li><li data-section-id="1bfo3du" data-start="1609" data-end="1680">Create opportunities for local clubs, charities and community groups.</li><li data-section-id="1upz41l" data-start="1681" data-end="1749">Remain sensitive to the landscape and the character of Goring Gap.</li><li data-section-id="rxdy3w" data-start="1750" data-end="1832">Can operate seasonally without permanently changing the open nature of the land.</li></ul><p data-start="1834" data-end="2028">This is an opportunity to think creatively about how a privately owned green space might provide genuine and lasting benefits for the wider community while remaining environmentally responsible.</p><p data-start="2030" data-end="2234">The land will not be built upon or permanently developed. You have our word. Please print this page and keep it safe! Our intention is to preserve its open character while finding thoughtful, sustainable and inclusive ways for local people of all ages to enjoy it. And to also help our beloved Worthing find its way and encourage tourisim. </p><p data-start="2236" data-end="2472" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">If planning permission is granted, we will publish details of how residents and community organisations can submit their ideas. We would love the future of the site to be shaped not only by us, but by the people it is intended to serve. In the meantime please use the contact button above. We would love to hear your ideas. Thank you.</p>								</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-4c3668b e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-2ff94d6 " data-id="4c3668b" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="4c3668b">
    		<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-f3ed238 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="f3ed238" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<h5 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">01 August 2026 - The Green Party Worthing</h5>				</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-0700c34 e-con e-atomic-element e-flexbox-base e-default-div e-f5a1e59 " data-id="0700c34" data-element_type="e-flexbox" data-e-type="e-flexbox" data-interaction-id="0700c34">
    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-3353979 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="3353979" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-da3063d elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="da3063d" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p class="isSelectedEnd">The Green Party leaflet has just dropped through people&#8217;s letterboxes and, unsurprisingly, we feature in it—sadly in a negative light. You can read it for yourself <a href="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/IMG_9588-1-scaled.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">here</a>.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">What the leaflet fails to mention are our environmental and public safety credentials.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">We now operate using <strong>100% green energy</strong> and have eliminated all fossil fuel use from our business. We actively promote biodiversity, support local community initiatives, prioritise local suppliers wherever possible, provide employment opportunities for young people, and use biodegradable and compostable products throughout our operation wherever we can. Wherever possible, we also serve locally sourced craft beers, wines, spirits, soft drinks, smoothies, tea, coffee and ice cream.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">We recycle wherever possible, continually look for ways to reduce waste, and use electric vehicles to transport stock to and from the site. We plant trees to offset our remaining carbon footprint and even cut our grass using electric lawn mowers, all charged on site by our own solar panels. You would struggle to find a greener small business anywhere in Worthing—or indeed across West Sussex.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">These are not promises for the future. They are actions we have already taken because we genuinely care about protecting our environment and are passionate about both Worthing and Goring Gap.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">Despite this, the only political party to have publicly objected to our planning application is the Green Party. Since then, a small number of people online, who appear to have an agenda against us, have regularly posted misinformation about our business.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">We have even experienced strangers coming onto or around our premises and approaching customers as they leave, questioning why they are supporting our business. We find this behaviour deeply concerning and completely unnecessary.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">Much of the political criticism of our operation has come from Claire Hunt and other local Green Party representatives, and the leaflet reproduced above is yet another example of what we believe has become an increasingly negative, obsessive and personal campaign against us over the last three years by Claire Hunt. You can read her submissions <a href="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/All-Complaints-from-Claire-Hunt-and-leaflet.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">here</a>. No one else, other than a few mad hatters in Ferring, have been so blinkered in their determination to stop us revitalising and using abandoned land for the good of the community and tourisim. As one 6 year old recently said, when asking why we do not have any sand in our sandpit, &#8216;what is their problem?&#8217; We didn&#8217;t have an answer.</p><p>Whatever people&#8217;s views on our planning application, political opposition should never spill over into personal hostility, misinformation or the intimidation of customers who simply choose to visit and support a local business.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">We prefer to let our actions speak for themselves. Since opening, there has been no anti-social behaviour, no light or noise pollution—just families, residents and visitors enjoying one of the most beautiful locations on the Sussex coast. Basically non of the predictions in Claire Hunts written objections. See <a href="https://www.goringgap.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/All-Complaints-from-Claire-Hunt-and-leaflet.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">here</a>.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">So let&#8217;s turn this around. The leaflet states that Claire Hunt is working hard for a greener, fairer and safer Goring. Yet the same leaflet explains that she and other Green Party councillors have objected to our planning application, which includes clean toilets, baby-changing facilities and the only publicly accessible lifesaving defibrillator on Goring Gap.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">That raises two simple questions:</p><p class="isSelectedEnd"><strong>1. Which should take greater priority—providing clean toilet and baby-changing facilities for families, or leaving the current situation unchanged?</strong></p><p class="isSelectedEnd"><strong>2. Is having the only publicly accessible lifesaving defibrillator on Goring Gap a benefit to public safety, or not?</strong></p><p class="isSelectedEnd">Is there anything more precious than a newborn baby? Most parents would probably say there is not. We believe every parent deserves access to a clean, safe and hygienic place to change their baby&#8217;s nappy. That is not a luxury—it is a basic facility that families should reasonably expect when visiting Goring.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">Below are photographs of the toilet and baby-changing facilities currently provided by Worthing Borough Council <span style="font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400;">at Goring Gap</span><span style="font-size: 16px;">, under the stewardship of Claire Hunt (as Ward Councillor) and the Green Party, alongside the facilities we have installed for local families and visitors.</span></p><p class="isSelectedEnd">Claire Hunt has publicly called for our business to be closed and has publically objected to our planning application, which includes these health and safety facilities. She has also called on Worthing Borough Council to take enforcement action against our business, which could ultimately result in the closure of our toilets, baby-changing facilities and the removal of the publicly accessible defibrillator.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">We believe it is reasonable for residents to ask whether removing these facilities would improve public safety or reduce it?</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">You can therefore decide for yourself whether the existing Council facilities, under the watch of Claire Hunt and the Green Party, are fit for purpose, or whether the facilities we have provided offer a greater benefit to local families, visitors and the wider community.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">We are also extremely proud to have recently been awarded the highest possible <strong>Food Hygiene Rating of 5</strong>—something that reflects our commitment to cleanliness, hygiene and high standards. You can read more about that <a href="https://ratings.food.gov.uk/business/1955241/goring-gap-worthing" target="_blank" rel="noopener">here</a>.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">Ultimately, we will let you draw your own conclusions.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">The photographs below have not been edited, enhanced or staged. They simply show the Council facilities currently available at Goring Gap alongside those we have provided as part of our business, allowing everyone to compare the two and make up their own minds.</p><p>Click on the images to enlarge them and decide for yourself whether the reality reflects the claims made in the Green Party leaflet. Thank you.</p>								</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		
</div>
